[Opening "Italian Game: Evans Gambit"]
[Start "[0,0,0]"]
[Orientation "black"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 {Giri flags the Evans Gambit as the practical cost of choosing the early ...Bc5 move order. It is only one weak-file entry here, so treat this as an emergency reminder rather than the main Italian study line.} 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Ba5 6. d4 exd4 {Keep the deck's reference move. Black accepts, retreats, then opens the centre before White gets a free attacking setup.} 7. O-O Nf6 8. e5 d5 9. exf6 dxc4 {If White keeps throwing pawns forward, answer with central counterplay and remove the c4 bishop. Your priority is development and king safety, not hoarding every pawn.} *
